1
00:00:02,330 --> 00:00:04,000
Bye-bye.

2
00:00:04,370 --> 00:00:06,500
I just got reservations at Michelle's...

3
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:08,960
...and tickets to The Music Man to celebrate...

4
00:00:09,130 --> 00:00:11,670
...our first holiday as a betrothed couple.

5
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:15,050
"Betrothed."

6
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:15,050
Betrothed couple.

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,140
Hey.

8
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,140
Hi.

9
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,180
Aw.

10
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,180
Oh.

11
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:25,060
Pheebs?

12
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:25,060
Uh-huh?

13
00:00:25,230 --> 00:00:26,810
Skull?

14
00:00:26,980 --> 00:00:28,310
Oh. Yeah, it's my mom's.

15
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:30,070
Oh, my God!

16
00:00:30,730 --> 00:00:32,780
No, no, no. It's not my mom.

17
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:34,610
It belonged to my mom.

18
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:38,280
She used to put it out every Christmas...

19
00:00:38,450 --> 00:00:42,790
...to remind us that even though it's Christmas, people still die.

20
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:46,330
And you can put candy in it.

21
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:50,710
Hey.

22
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:50,710
Hey.

23
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:51,920
Licorice?

24
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:55,130
Sure. Ha, ha.

25
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:58,840
I get Ben for the holidays this year.

26
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:58,840
That's great!

27
00:00:59,010 --> 00:01:01,430
Are you gonna dress up as Santa?

28
00:00:59,010 --> 00:01:01,430
Nope.

29
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:03,430
I know Susan does every year.

30
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:06,520
I want to take this year to teach him about Hanukkah.

31
00:01:06,690 --> 00:01:08,150
And maybe I could teach Ben...

32
00:01:08,310 --> 00:01:11,150
...about the Christmas skull and how people die.

33
00:01:11,650 --> 00:01:14,490
You may need to use this year to teach Ben about Phoebe.

34
00:01:14,650 --> 00:01:15,940
Mm.

35
00:01:19,320 --> 00:01:20,780
Hey.

36
00:01:26,290 --> 00:01:28,620
Did you know he was in there?

37
00:01:26,290 --> 00:01:28,620
No.

38
00:01:30,210 --> 00:01:32,880
How long have we been home?

39
00:01:30,210 --> 00:01:32,880
About half an hour.

40
00:01:33,050 --> 00:01:34,340
Lovely.

41
00:02:15,210 --> 00:02:18,220
You know what I was thinking? When we get married, will you, uh...

42
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:20,010
...change your name to "Bing"?

43
00:02:21,050 --> 00:02:22,550
No.

44
00:02:23,930 --> 00:02:24,970
Why not?

45
00:02:26,270 --> 00:02:27,720
Bing's weird.

46
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:30,890
Oh, hey, you guys.

47
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:32,810
Hey.

48
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:32,810
Hey

49
00:02:32,980 --> 00:02:34,230
Guess what?

50
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:37,230
My landlord just called. My apartment's gonna be ready soon.

51
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:38,780
I guess I'll be moving out.

52
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:40,650
Aw, Phoebe, I'm gonna miss you.

53
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:42,740
Yes, you will be very sad.

54
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:48,500
I gotta go tell Rachel the good news.

55
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:48,500
Oh. You'll be living together again?

56
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:51,370
Why not?

57
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:51,370
She's having so much fun with Joey...

58
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:53,880
...I assumed she'd still be living with him.

59
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:56,710
Why do you think she's having so much fun?

60
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:59,210
No reason, except she...

61
00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:01,180
...told me.

62
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:04,090
She said she didn't want to live with me?

63
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:07,010
No. No, she didn't say that.

64
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:10,350
I think you should talk to Monica now.

65
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:14,150
Phoebe, I'm sure she wants to live with you.

66
00:03:14,310 --> 00:03:15,860
You're absolutely sure?

67
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:18,530
No, but I'll bet she probably does.

68
00:03:18,690 --> 00:03:19,820
Oh, probably?

69
00:03:20,030 --> 00:03:21,320
I don't like that word.

70
00:03:23,070 --> 00:03:26,240
I know what "probably" really means. Yeah, uh-huh, yeah.

71
00:03:26,450 --> 00:03:28,740
"Oh, your mom probably won't kill herself."

72
00:03:28,910 --> 00:03:32,710
You know. I'm sorry, but I'm not hanging my hopes...

73
00:03:32,870 --> 00:03:36,340
...of Rachel and I living together on "probably."

74
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:39,130
You gotta take care of yourself in this world.

75
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:41,840
History teaches us nothing.

76
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:47,010
Bing doesn't seem so weird now, does it?

77
00:03:52,270 --> 00:03:53,770
You're home.

78
00:03:53,940 --> 00:03:55,650
Guess what Phoebe got me for Christmas?

79
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:07,530
Drums?

80
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:07,530
No, drums!

81
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:16,170
Could we get two burritos to go, please? Ha, ha.

82
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:22,210
I'm sorry. But not that sorry, you don't have to live with it.

83
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:24,880
Um, we have a reservation under Bing.

84
00:04:25,050 --> 00:04:28,470
Okay, we'll have a table for you in about 45 minutes.

85
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:31,640
We have tickets to The Music Man at 8.

86
00:04:31,810 --> 00:04:34,640
I'm sorry. Christmas is a very busy time, sir.

87
00:04:34,850 --> 00:04:37,100
Is this because of the burrito thing?

88
00:04:39,610 --> 00:04:42,940
You need to give him money.

89
00:04:39,610 --> 00:04:42,940
Give him money? It was a joke!

90
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:46,780
To get a table. Places like this are always shaking you down.

91
00:04:46,950 --> 00:04:50,450
Everybody wants a payoff.

92
00:04:46,950 --> 00:04:50,450
All right, calm down, O'Malley.

93
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:55,710
I'll slip him some money.

94
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:55,710
But you've got to be smooth.

95
00:04:55,870 --> 00:04:58,130
Hey, I can be smooth.

96
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:05,380
We're in a hurry. If you could get us a table...

97
00:05:05,550 --> 00:05:07,300
...a bit quicker, I'd appreciate it.

98
00:05:07,470 --> 00:05:09,720
Of course, sir.

99
00:05:07,470 --> 00:05:09,720
Okay.

100
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:14,640
How'd it go?

101
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:14,640
Had the money in the wrong hand.

102
00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:22,980
You don't feel...

103
00:05:23,150 --> 00:05:24,820
...like you're gonna throw up?

104
00:05:23,150 --> 00:05:24,820
No.

105
00:05:24,990 --> 00:05:27,610
Well, I do. So let's...

106
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:31,330
So, Ben, you, uh...

107
00:05:31,490 --> 00:05:33,990
You know what holiday is coming up?

108
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:35,200
Christmas.

109
00:05:35,370 --> 00:05:38,580
Yeah, and you know what other holiday is coming up?

110
00:05:38,750 --> 00:05:40,130
Christmas Eve.

111
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:44,090
Yes, but also...

112
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:47,050
Hanukkah!

113
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:52,050
See, you're part Jewish and Hanukkah is a Jewish holiday.

114
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:54,930
Santa has reindeers that can fly.

115
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:56,560
Right, um, but on Hanukkah...

116
00:05:56,770 --> 00:05:59,190
Hanukkah is a celebration of a miracle.

117
00:05:59,350 --> 00:06:03,070
Years and years ago there were these people called the Maccabees.

118
00:06:03,230 --> 00:06:04,650
Jingle bells, jingle bells

119
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:06,610
Okay, that's right. Yes...

120
00:06:06,820 --> 00:06:09,530
...but on Hanukkah, we sing, uh:

121
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:12,570
Dreidel, dreidel, dreidel I made you out of clay

122
00:06:12,870 --> 00:06:15,410
Rudolph the red-nosed reindeer

123
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:18,250
Ha, ha. Okay, it's not a contest.

124
00:06:18,410 --> 00:06:20,120
When is Santa coming?

125
00:06:21,290 --> 00:06:24,880
How about this year, instead of Santa...

126
00:06:25,090 --> 00:06:27,800
...we have fun celebrating Hanukkah?

127
00:06:27,970 --> 00:06:29,880
No Santa?

128
00:06:30,050 --> 00:06:31,680
Was I bad?

129
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:35,930
No, no, no, you weren't bad. You've been very good, Ben.

130
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:39,480
Santa's mad at me.

131
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:39,480
No, hey, hey, come on.

132
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:42,060
Ben, Santa is not mad at you, okay?

133
00:06:42,270 --> 00:06:44,440
You're his favorite little guy.

134
00:06:44,610 --> 00:06:46,110
So Santa's coming?

135
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:49,900
Yes!

136
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:51,780
Santa's coming.

137
00:06:56,490 --> 00:06:58,870
It's easy. Just keep it casual.

138
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:02,580
Shake his hand and give him the money.

139
00:07:02,750 --> 00:07:05,880
How do you know so much about this?

140
00:07:02,750 --> 00:07:05,880
I don't know.

141
00:07:06,420 --> 00:07:08,710
Richard used to do it, didn't he?

142
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:11,930
We'd be eating our soup right now.

143
00:07:12,470 --> 00:07:15,390
Mustached bastard.

144
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:20,310
Those people just left. Come on. Quick, give him the money.

145
00:07:20,890 --> 00:07:21,940
Excuse me.

146
00:07:29,110 --> 00:07:31,400
We're in a bit of a hurry. Can we please?

147
00:07:31,570 --> 00:07:33,410
Ah-ha-ha-ha.

148
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:48,630
Ha!

149
00:07:50,090 --> 00:07:52,170
So you like the drums.

150
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:54,300
That's great.

151
00:07:56,010 --> 00:07:58,180
I was worried that they would create maybe...

152
00:07:58,350 --> 00:08:00,680
...an unbearable living situation.

153
00:08:00,850 --> 00:08:04,940
But, okay, well, apparently not. So, yay!

154
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:07,360
Hey, we already learned a song.

155
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:10,860
Ready? One, two, three, four.

156
00:08:12,650 --> 00:08:14,530
Tequila!

157
00:08:16,870 --> 00:08:18,620
That's fun.

158
00:08:25,330 --> 00:08:26,500
Here you go.

159
00:08:26,670 --> 00:08:29,130
Thank you, Gunther. Put her there.

160
00:08:31,670 --> 00:08:34,420
Definitely not easier with coins.

161
00:08:35,510 --> 00:08:37,090
Thank you.

162
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:41,060
Hey, Pheebs.

163
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:41,060
Hey.

164
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:44,480
Here. Now I only owe you $49.50.

165
00:08:45,770 --> 00:08:47,100
Hey, Pheebs.

166
00:08:45,770 --> 00:08:47,100
Hey.

167
00:08:47,310 --> 00:08:51,110
If you want to get Joey a gift that disrupts the entire building...

168
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:53,400
...why not something more subtle...

169
00:08:53,610 --> 00:08:54,860
...like a wrecking ball...

170
00:08:55,030 --> 00:08:58,570
...or a vial of smallpox to release in the hallway?

171
00:08:58,780 --> 00:09:01,700
It's not just the drum noise. Every five minutes...

172
00:09:01,910 --> 00:09:03,750
...Joey throws his sticks in the air...

173
00:09:03,910 --> 00:09:07,370
...and I have to hear: "Oh, my eye! Oh, God, my eye!"

174
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:10,170
I mean, it's so annoying.

175
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:10,170
Yes, thank you.

176
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:14,970
You see, this is how normal people are supposed to react to drums.

177
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:19,010
You got Joey drums to annoy Rachel...

178
00:09:19,180 --> 00:09:21,640
...so she wouldn't want to live there anymore?

179
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:23,930
Maybe on some level.

180
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:35,650
You could just not throw the sticks up in the air.

181
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:37,860
What is rock 'n' roll about that?

182
00:09:39,490 --> 00:09:42,910
Hey, Joey, I got you another present.

183
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:46,660
Hold it! Before you tell me what it is...

184
00:09:50,330 --> 00:09:51,790
Okay, what is it?

185
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:53,130
It's a...

186
00:09:53,340 --> 00:09:54,590
...tarantula!

187
00:09:57,630 --> 00:09:59,010
Oh.

188
00:10:00,260 --> 00:10:03,970
God, Rachel, I'm sorry. What was I thinking...

189
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:07,310
...giving Joey this big, gross, scary spider...

190
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:11,230
...in such a poorly constructed cage?

191
00:10:11,730 --> 00:10:14,480
What are you talking about? I love them.

192
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:20,530
I had a tarantula when I was a kid. But it died because my cat ate it.

193
00:10:20,700 --> 00:10:23,370
And then my cat died.

194
00:10:23,950 --> 00:10:25,660
But, Joey, isn't this cool?

195
00:10:25,830 --> 00:10:28,580
Is it on me? I feel like it's on me. I got...

196
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:33,080
Oh, isn't that adorable?

197
00:10:33,290 --> 00:10:36,550
Joey is afraid of the tarantula.

198
00:10:33,290 --> 00:10:36,550
Oh.

199
00:10:36,710 --> 00:10:38,010
He's so adorable.

200
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:39,550
He's so much fun.

201
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:42,390
I'm glad you're having so much fun here.

202
00:10:42,550 --> 00:10:44,050
Whoa. Wait a minute.

203
00:10:44,220 --> 00:10:45,260
What's the matter?

204
00:10:45,930 --> 00:10:47,600
Our apartment is ready.

205
00:10:48,270 --> 00:10:52,350
And that makes you angry because?

206
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:55,150
Because you'd rather live here with Joey.

207
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:58,030
Where did you get that?

208
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:58,030
Monica and Chandler...

209
00:10:58,240 --> 00:11:00,570
...said you were having so much fun here...

210
00:11:00,780 --> 00:11:05,490
...and apparently no amount of drums or tarantulas is gonna change that.

211
00:11:07,910 --> 00:11:09,750
Did you get all this stuff for Joey...

212
00:11:09,910 --> 00:11:12,250
...to try to drive me out of the apartment?

213
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:15,920
You might as well have gotten him a fish.

214
00:11:16,090 --> 00:11:18,380
You know how fish freak me out.

215
00:11:19,510 --> 00:11:21,220
Fish.

216
00:11:22,130 --> 00:11:25,350
But it wouldn't have mattered. We're gonna live together.

217
00:11:25,550 --> 00:11:27,430
That's the deal.

218
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,890
Yes, but I wanted you to want to live with me.

219
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:32,850
But if you're having so much fun over here...

220
00:11:33,020 --> 00:11:35,190
Oh. It's so much more fun with you.

221
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:38,150
We did have fun, didn't we?

222
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:38,150
We did.

223
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:41,490
They say if we want, we could see it tonight.

224
00:11:41,650 --> 00:11:43,780
I would love to.

225
00:11:41,650 --> 00:11:43,780
Yay, okay!

226
00:11:43,950 --> 00:11:46,950
Good, good, good.

227
00:11:43,950 --> 00:11:46,950
Great. All right. Good.

228
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:49,910
And Monica asked me to make the drumming stop.

229
00:11:50,910 --> 00:11:53,710
Um, ahem.

230
00:11:55,290 --> 00:11:56,670
Done.

231
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:03,760
Hey.

232
00:12:03,930 --> 00:12:06,260
Hello, sir. You here to return those pants?

233
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:14,810
No, these are my pants.

234
00:12:15,230 --> 00:12:16,440
Oh.

235
00:12:16,610 --> 00:12:18,150
Okay.

236
00:12:18,650 --> 00:12:22,400
How can I help you?

237
00:12:18,650 --> 00:12:22,400
Um, do you have a Santa outfit left?

238
00:12:22,570 --> 00:12:24,780
Two days before Christmas? Sorry, man.

239
00:12:25,110 --> 00:12:28,950
Okay, look. Do you have anything, uh, Christmas-y?

240
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:32,000
I promised my son, and I really don't want to disappoint him.

241
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:36,330
Um, come on, you gotta have something.

242
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:39,500
I'm the Holiday Armadillo!

243
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:43,630
I'm a friend of Santa's...

244
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:46,630
...and he sent me here to wish you...

245
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:50,050
...a merry Christmas!

246
00:12:50,810 --> 00:12:54,390
What happened to Santa, Holiday Armadillo?

247
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:57,980
Santa was unavailable...

248
00:12:58,150 --> 00:13:01,110
...so close to Christmas.

249
00:13:02,110 --> 00:13:03,650
Come in, have a seat.

250
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:07,780
You must be exhausted, coming all the way from Texas.

251
00:13:10,870 --> 00:13:13,200
Texas?

252
00:13:10,870 --> 00:13:13,200
That's right, Ben.

253
00:13:13,370 --> 00:13:15,160
I'm Santa's representative...

254
00:13:15,370 --> 00:13:19,250
...for all the Southern states.

255
00:13:19,420 --> 00:13:22,750
And Mexico!

256
00:13:24,130 --> 00:13:25,720
But Santa sent me here...

257
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:29,550
...to give you these presents, Ben.

258
00:13:29,760 --> 00:13:33,260
Maybe the lady will help me with these presents.

259
00:13:48,490 --> 00:13:49,700
Wow, thanks!

260
00:13:49,910 --> 00:13:51,320
You're welcome, Ben.

261
00:13:51,490 --> 00:13:54,410
Merry Christmas. Ooh.

262
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:58,210
And happy Hanukkah!

263
00:13:59,330 --> 00:14:02,670
Are you for Hanukkah too? Because I'm part Jewish.

264
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:06,170
You are? Me too.

265
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:10,970
Because armadillos also wandered in the desert?

266
00:14:12,890 --> 00:14:15,220
You want to wander in the hall?

267
00:14:16,980 --> 00:14:19,100
Oh. Hey, Ben!

268
00:14:19,270 --> 00:14:21,480
What if the Holiday Armadillo...

269
00:14:21,690 --> 00:14:25,280
...told you all about the Festival of Lights?

270
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:26,530
Cool!

271
00:14:26,690 --> 00:14:28,280
Come on, Ben.

272
00:14:31,490 --> 00:14:33,950
Years and years ago...

273
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:36,410
...there were these people called...

274
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:38,080
...the Maccabees!

275
00:14:38,250 --> 00:14:41,790
Ho-ho-ho. Merry Christmas!

276
00:14:43,590 --> 00:14:44,630
Santa!

277
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,210
Hey.

278
00:14:47,170 --> 00:14:50,050
What are you doing here, Santa?

279
00:14:52,140 --> 00:14:54,800
Well, I'm here to see my old buddy, Ben.

280
00:14:55,470 --> 00:14:57,180
What are you doing here...

281
00:14:57,390 --> 00:15:01,190
...Weird Turtle Man?

282
00:15:03,060 --> 00:15:05,940
I'm the Holiday Armadillo...

283
00:15:06,150 --> 00:15:09,530
...your part-Jewish friend.

284
00:15:10,990 --> 00:15:14,780
You sent me here to give Ben some presents.

285
00:15:14,950 --> 00:15:16,870
Remember?

286
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:19,250
What?

287
00:15:22,290 --> 00:15:24,460
Did you bring me any presents, Santa?

288
00:15:24,630 --> 00:15:26,340
You bet I did, Ben.

289
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:28,550
Put her there.

290
00:15:32,890 --> 00:15:37,930
Well, it would have worked this time if his hands weren't so damn small.

291
00:15:40,350 --> 00:15:43,270
Ho-ho-ho.

292
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:45,100
Ben, come open more presents.

293
00:15:45,270 --> 00:15:48,190
Santa, the armadillo and I will have a talk in the kitchen.

294
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:51,490
There's a sentence I never thought I'd say.

295
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:54,700
What are you doing?

296
00:15:54,870 --> 00:15:58,120
You said you were having trouble finding a Santa costume...

297
00:15:58,290 --> 00:16:00,790
...so I borrowed one from a guy at work.

298
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:03,580
Thank you, but you gotta leave.

299
00:16:03,750 --> 00:16:05,250
Why?

300
00:16:03,750 --> 00:16:05,250
Because...

301
00:16:05,420 --> 00:16:08,130
...I'm finally getting him excited about Hanukkah...

302
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:09,840
...and you're wrecking it.

303
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:14,130
But I didn't get to shake my belly like a bowlful of jelly.

304
00:16:17,220 --> 00:16:21,100
I'm sorry, Chandler, but this is really important to me.

305
00:16:22,020 --> 00:16:25,350
Fine, I'll give the suit back.

306
00:16:25,850 --> 00:16:29,520
Hey, you think you can keep it another night?

307
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:33,740
Santa, really?

308
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:35,740
Yeah, is that okay?

309
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:39,580
Did your dad ever dress up like Santa?

310
00:16:40,790 --> 00:16:44,120
No.

311
00:16:40,790 --> 00:16:44,120
Then it's okay!

312
00:16:45,290 --> 00:16:47,580
Okay, Ben. Santa has to go.

313
00:16:47,750 --> 00:16:49,340
Say goodbye.

314
00:16:49,500 --> 00:16:52,170
No, why does he have to go?

315
00:16:52,340 --> 00:16:56,630
Because if Santa and the Holiday...

316
00:16:57,010 --> 00:16:58,800
...Armadillo...

317
00:17:00,890 --> 00:17:03,310
...are ever in the same room for too long...

318
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:06,640
...the universe will implode!

319
00:17:08,230 --> 00:17:10,610
Merry Christmas!

320
00:17:12,030 --> 00:17:15,900
No, why can't the armadillo leave? I want Santa.

321
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:19,990
Fine, I give up. Santa...

322
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:22,740
Santa can stay!

323
00:17:24,660 --> 00:17:25,710
Well, I'll stay...

324
00:17:25,910 --> 00:17:29,460
...but only because I want to hear about Hanukkah.

325
00:17:30,290 --> 00:17:32,800
Ben, will you sit here with Santa...

326
00:17:32,960 --> 00:17:35,210
...and learn about Hanukkah?

327
00:17:35,380 --> 00:17:37,510
Okay, Santa.

328
00:17:38,470 --> 00:17:40,050
Thank you.

329
00:17:38,470 --> 00:17:40,050
You're welcome.

330
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:42,350
All right, it's time...

331
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:45,850
...for the story of Hanukkah.

332
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:48,140
Years and years ago...

333
00:17:48,310 --> 00:17:52,190
...there were these people called the Maccabees!

334
00:17:52,650 --> 00:17:54,860
Merry Christmas!

335
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:08,160
Oh, wow, look at this place!

336
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:12,540
Oh, this is terrible.

337
00:18:12,710 --> 00:18:14,210
They've made so many changes...

338
00:18:14,380 --> 00:18:17,760
...I can't even feel my grandmother's presence anymore.

339
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:20,470
Oh, new sconces!

340
00:18:21,430 --> 00:18:23,180
Oh, my God!

341
00:18:21,430 --> 00:18:23,180
What?

342
00:18:23,850 --> 00:18:27,480
Remember, uh, how you told me your grandmother put up that wall...

343
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:29,940
...to make that into two bedrooms?

344
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:29,940
Yeah.

345
00:18:30,100 --> 00:18:32,400
And that the landlord might find out...

346
00:18:32,610 --> 00:18:34,730
...and then tear it down?

347
00:18:32,610 --> 00:18:34,730
Yeah?

348
00:18:35,570 --> 00:18:38,030
Do you really not know where I'm going?

349
00:18:39,070 --> 00:18:40,820
It left. It's one huge room.

350
00:18:41,030 --> 00:18:43,070
Oh, no!

351
00:18:45,290 --> 00:18:47,040
Wow!

352
00:18:48,330 --> 00:18:49,540
See?

353
00:18:49,710 --> 00:18:52,420
I guess we'll have to put the wall back up.

354
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:56,630
You can't because of the new skylight.

355
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:56,630
There's a skylight?

356
00:18:57,380 --> 00:18:58,760
Wow!

357
00:18:59,510 --> 00:19:03,090
Oh. So should we start looking for a new place?

358
00:19:06,430 --> 00:19:07,930
You know, I'm sensing...

359
00:19:08,100 --> 00:19:12,190
...that, um, my grandmother would not be comfortable with that.

360
00:19:13,690 --> 00:19:14,900
Oh, yeah?

361
00:19:15,110 --> 00:19:18,070
Starting to feel her again there, are we?

362
00:19:18,690 --> 00:19:20,990
A little bit. Yeah.

363
00:19:18,690 --> 00:19:20,990
Yeah.

364
00:19:22,110 --> 00:19:25,870
Is your grandmother maybe saying that you should live here alone?

365
00:19:26,030 --> 00:19:28,290
You heard it too? You have the gift.

366
00:19:29,910 --> 00:19:31,870
Phoebe, it's okay.

367
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:34,250
I like living with Joey.

368
00:19:34,420 --> 00:19:36,880
Are you sure?

369
00:19:34,420 --> 00:19:36,880
Please. I hate packing...

370
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:38,590
...it's closer to work.

371
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:41,050
And we do have fun.

372
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:45,430
Although, I'm really gonna miss living with you.

373
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:47,930
Oh, me too.

374
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:47,930
I know.

375
00:19:49,810 --> 00:19:51,680
Oh. Did you hear that?

376
00:19:51,850 --> 00:19:54,060
I'm getting something from your grandmother.

377
00:19:54,230 --> 00:19:57,570
She said since you get to keep the one-bedroom apartment...

378
00:19:57,730 --> 00:20:01,280
...you should give Rachel the purple chair.

379
00:20:03,570 --> 00:20:05,950
No, I do not hear that.

380
00:20:07,370 --> 00:20:10,620
And the miracle was that that little bit of oil...

381
00:20:10,790 --> 00:20:14,670
...that should have lasted just one day, burned for...

382
00:20:14,830 --> 00:20:16,790
Eight whole days.

383
00:20:14,830 --> 00:20:16,790
That's right.

384
00:20:16,960 --> 00:20:20,840
And that's why we celebrate Hanukkah today. The end.

385
00:20:21,010 --> 00:20:23,050
Awesome.

386
00:20:21,010 --> 00:20:23,050
Yeah.

387
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:24,470
My favorite part...

388
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:29,260
...was when Superman flew all the Jews out of Egypt.

389
00:20:33,020 --> 00:20:37,940
The armadillo was actually not so thrilled about that part.

390
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:41,070
Okay, Ben, it's time to light...

391
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:44,400
...the Hanukkah candles!

392
00:20:44,570 --> 00:20:46,200
Ho-ho-ho.

393
00:20:53,210 --> 00:20:54,250
Hey.

394
00:20:54,410 --> 00:20:55,790
Oh.

395
00:20:54,410 --> 00:20:55,790
Wow.

396
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:58,420
Looks like the Easter Bunny's funeral in here.

397
00:21:01,550 --> 00:21:03,880
Come on, come on. We're lighting the candles.

398
00:21:04,050 --> 00:21:05,630
Oh, oh.

399
00:21:09,180 --> 00:21:10,930
I understand why Superman is here...

400
00:21:11,100 --> 00:21:14,930
...but why is there a porcupine at the Easter Bunny's funeral?

401
00:21:23,150 --> 00:21:25,650
You get it?

402
00:21:23,150 --> 00:21:25,650
I got it.

403
00:21:25,820 --> 00:21:27,700
Back in the cage?

404
00:21:28,780 --> 00:21:30,910
It's back in the cage.

405
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:32,950
Is the cage closed?

406
00:21:34,660 --> 00:21:37,920
Joey, will you just come out here and stop being such a baby?

